{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "17", "x": 0.9084862262338186, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.025257022369817146, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "been identified, in counties such as Cambridgeshire, that are hundreds of years", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.12319506908974809, "w": 0.8259462822555039, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "old, and have mysteriously escaped the epidemic.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.15152541916388573, "w": 0.5072822705750409, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "The key, Russell says, is to identify and study those trees that have survived and", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.1896453759080105, "w": 0.8258376058044707, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "work out why they stood tall when millions of others succumbed. Nevertheless,", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.21797572598214812, "w": 0.8260988393867654, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "opportunities are limited as the number of these mature survivors is relatively", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.24630607605628574, "w": 0.8266480655642978, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "small. 'What are the reasons for their survival?' asks Russell. 'Avoidance,", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2746735439806541, "w": 0.8260988393867654, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "tolerance, resistance? We don't know where the balance lies between the three. I", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3030039694975767, "w": 0.8263168074385545, "h": 0.018822616509687834, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "don't see how it can be entirely down to luck.'", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.33133430071101805, "w": 0.46636312616218445, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "D", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.36945418201235786, "w": 0.02101269433220525, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "For centuries, elm ran a close second to oak as the hardwood tree of choice", "x": 0.16774843308549978, "y": 0.36945418201235786, "w": 0.7659426303166493, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "in Britain and was in many instances the most prominent tree in the landscape.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.39778456980788796, "w": 0.8258376058044707, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Not only was elm common in European forests, it became a key component of", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4261149576034181, "w": 0.826077001571605, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "birch, ash and hazel woodlands. The use of elm is thought to go back to the Bronze", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4544453076775557, "w": 0.8267349042001706, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Age, when it was widely used for tools. Elm was also the preferred material for", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.48280040298518045, "w": 0.8259682225956181, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "shields and early swords. In the 18th century, it was planted more widely and its", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5111307907807106, "w": 0.8259245469652973, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "wood was used for items such as storage crates and flooring. It was also suitable", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5394611408548482, "w": 0.8266336095458113, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "for items that experienced high levels of impact and was used to build the keel of", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5677915286503784, "w": 0.8262733368581412, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "the 19th-century sailing ship Cutty Sark as well as mining equipment.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5961219164459085, "w": 0.7058813593537565, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "E", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6343901559839935, "w": 0.01919854090586743, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Given how ingrained elm is in British culture, it's unsurprising the tree has", "x": 0.16774843308549978, "y": 0.6343901559839935, "w": 0.7656008121206641, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "many advocates. Amongst them is Peter Bourne of the National Elm Collection in", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6627576239083618, "w": 0.8260940207139367, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Brighton. 'I saw Dutch elm disease unfold as a small boy,' he says. 'The elm", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6909396534671467, "w": 0.8266433494164228, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "seemed to be part of rural England, but I remember watching trees just lose their", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7192700035412843, "w": 0.8261744002777196, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "leaves and that really stayed with me.' Today, the city of Brighton's elms total", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.747600429058207, "w": 0.8261159610540508, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "about 17,000. Local factors appear to have contributed to their survival. Strong", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7759307791323447, "w": 0.8258813839597454, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "winds from the sea make it difficult for the determined elm bark beetle to attack", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8042611292064822, "w": 0.8259682225956181, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "this coastal city's elm population. However, the situation is precarious. 'The", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8325914792806198, "w": 0.8263860117823727, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "beetles can just march in if we're not careful, as the threat is right on our", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8609465745882446, "w": 0.8258811789098378, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "doorstep,' says Bourne.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8892770001051672, "w": 0.2417779856983841, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}